00:51:18,260 --> 00:51:24,260
The Killer is a 2023 American action thriller film directed by David
Fincher from a screenplay by Andrew Kevin Walker.

11
00:56:26,086 --> 00:56:32,086
It is based on the French graphic novel series The Killer written by
Alexis "Matz" Nolent and illustrated by Luc Jacamon.

12
01:01:33,913 --> 01:01:39,913
The film stars Michael Fassbender in the main role alongside Arliss Howard, Charles Parnell,
Kerry O'Malley, Sala Baker, Sophie Charlotte, and Tilda Swinton in supporting roles.

13
01:06:41,739 --> 01:06:47,739
In the film, Fassbender plays an assassin who embarks on an
international vendetta after a hit goes wrong.

14
01:11:49,565 --> 01:11:55,565
Development on the graphic novel adaptation began in November 2007, when Fincher was reported to direct the film with Alessandro Camon
writing the script, and Paramount Pictures and Plan B Entertainment, respectively, were hired to distribute and produce the film.

15
01:16:57,391 --> 01:17:03,391
By February 2021, Fincher moved the project over to Netflix with Walker
replacing Camon as writer and Fassbender circling the lead role.

16
01:22:05,217 --> 01:22:11,217
Swinton joined the cast that October, with filming beginning
the following month, and wrapped March 2022.

17
01:27:13,043 --> 01:27:19,043
Filming locations included Paris, Dominican Republic,
and several places in the United States.

18
01:32:20,869 --> 01:32:26,869
The Killer premiered at the 80th Venice International
Film Festival on September 3, 2023.

19
01:37:28,695 --> 01:37:34,695
The film received a limited theatrical release on October 27
before streaming on Netflix on November 10.

20
01:42:36,521 --> 01:42:42,521
The film received positive reviews from critics.

21
01:47:44,347 --> 01:47:50,347
The film explores themes of sniper, new york city,
assassin, airport, paris, france.

22
01:52:52,173 --> 01:52:58,173
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
